From a16e9b0c2f3ef8a2063195ea829fa451894cc892 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 22:31:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] httpd/www: Reaper_Wireless diagnostics page

New native page (Wireless > Wireless Diagnostics) productizing the
2026-07-16 6 GHz investigation:

- Radio state per band: running vs configured chanspec, width, whether
  acsd owns the radio. One-click Lock pins the RUNNING chanspec through
  the stock start_apply path (wlN_chanspec + wlN_bw, restart_wireless),
  killing the per-boot acsd re-selection drift; Unlock returns to Auto.
- Channel-selection constraints panel: territory code, PSC state, and
  the live wlN_acs_excl_chans decoded entry-by-entry and matched
  verbatim against the four compiled-in exclusion lists (incl. the
  RT-BE96U 6726x-A1 10G-port WAR), so the operator can SEE what acsd
  is forbidden to pick and why.
- On-demand channel-quality capture: 1 Hz wl chanim_stats sampling for
  30-300 s to CSV in /tmp (RAM only, never syslog, never flash, no
  always-on sampler), with live nopkt/txop/glitch view and a verdict.
  This exact loop located a real 320 MHz interferer on metal: nopkt
  ~50% at 6g1/320-1 vs 1% at 6g1/160.

Backend do_reaper_wifi_cgi follows the reaper_traffic/rmcpd security
model: no request string reaches a shell; unit and duration are
allowlist-matched; the only popen variable is charset-checked
wlN_ifname; capture worker is a detached grandchild that stops by
run-token unlink, never by signal.

25 language dicts gain the RWIF_ block in lockstep (5631 lines each).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
